-- title:
--   Cokernel of a degree p^e isogeny on Cartier modules
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a field $k$ of characteristic $p$ that is perfect (in the sense of the `PerfectRing k p` instance), and let $d, e$ be natural numbers. Let $\Psi$ and $\Phi$ be $d$-dimensional formal group laws over $k$, each given by $d$ power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $X_i + Y_i$, and the associativity identity, and assume both are commutative. Let $\psi$ be a homomorphism $\Psi \to \Phi$, i.e. a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with zero constant term satisfying $\psi(\Psi(X,Y)) = \Phi(\psi(X),\psi(Y))$. Assume, first, that $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the components of $\psi$ has $k$-dimension exactly $p^e$, so that $\psi$ is an isogeny of degree $p^e$; and second, that the induced additive map $\psi_*$ on Cartier modules has cokernel killed by $p$: for every $f$ in `CartierModule p Φ` there is $g$ in `CartierModule p Ψ` with $\psi_* g = p \cdot f$, the action being that of $p \in W(k)$. Here `CartierModule p Φ` consists of $d$-tuples of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathbb{N}$, with zero constant term, compatible with the Witt addition laws and the group law $\Phi$, and $\psi_*$ is substitution of such a tuple into $\psi$. The conclusion is that the quotient of $M(\Phi)/pM(\Phi)$ by the $W(k)/(p)$-span of the classes of the elements $\psi_* g$ — that is, $M(\Phi)/\psi_* M(\Psi)$ — admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,e$ over the ring $W(k)/(p)$.
--
--   This is the degree formula for Cartier–Dieudonné modules in the case of an isogeny dividing $p$: an isogeny of degree $p^e$ induces a map of Cartier modules whose cokernel has length $e$, here recorded as freeness of rank $e$ over $W(k)/(p) \cong k$. It is the inductive engine behind the companion statement about Frobenius quotients, [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.exists_add_eq_and_nonempty_basis_quotient_span_frobenius_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.exists_add_eq_and_nonempty_basis_quotient_span_frobenius_of_finrank_eq_pow), and rests on the dévissage of $\psi$ through partial Frobenius quotients provided by [`MvFormalGroup.Hom.exists_comp_eq_and_comp_eq_X_pow_and_finrank_eq_pow_mul`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.Hom.exists_comp_eq_and_comp_eq_X_pow_and_finrank_eq_pow_mul).
